# The weekly keep-alive for the cohort reads. Install with:
#
#   scrontab release/01_cohort/scripts/slurm/freshen_reads.scron
#
# scrontab REPLACES the whole crontab, it does not append, so this file is the complete
# definition of llenzo's scheduled work. `scrontab -l` shows what is installed, `scrontab -r`
# removes everything. Slurm's cron is enabled here (ScronParameters = enable in slurm.conf),
# so no external scheduler and no ssh-from-a-laptop is involved: the trigger lives on the same
# machine as the data, and a laptop being asleep cannot break it.
#
# A scrontab job does NOT requeue if it fails; it simply runs again next week. With a 21-day
# purge window and a weekly cadence that is two free misses, which is the margin this needs.
#
# 06:00 Monday AWST. Off the Monday-morning login peak and well inside the copy partition's
# usual idle window.
#SCRON --account=pawsey1168
#SCRON --partition=copy
#SCRON --ntasks=1
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=4G
#SCRON --time=01:00:00
#SCRON --job-name=freshen_reads
#SCRON --output=/scratch/pawsey1168/llenzo/crypt/release/01_cohort/scripts/slurm/logs/freshen_cron_%j.out
#SCRON --error=/scratch/pawsey1168/llenzo/crypt/release/01_cohort/scripts/slurm/logs/freshen_cron_%j.err
0 6 * * 1 /scratch/pawsey1168/llenzo/crypt/release/01_cohort/scripts/slurm/freshen_reads.sh
